337 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c60cb50c-be28-51c2-98b8-1d31746b4a4e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478375 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186478337 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478375 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75107" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478375 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478375 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider $E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}]$ and a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ Find the row operation that, when applied to $A,$ is equivalent to multiplying $A$ by the given elementary matrix $E$ from the left." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478375 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0f630631-31e9-5df2-8934-f227dd41371f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478375 #edb/ref 1074 "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by multiplying the third row of ${I}_{3}$ by $\\frac{5}{4}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{5}{4}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary \nrow operation ${R}_{3}:=\\frac{5}{4}{R}_{3}$ to $A.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478383 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186478247 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478383 #edb/ref 1069 "q-110489" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478383 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478383 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that the following elementary row operations are applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ in the given order:\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:=(-1){R}_{3},\\,{R}_{2}↔{R}_{3}\n$$\n\nWhat is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478383 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "22a37135-efbb-5d81-a4c1-6f681fabaf48" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478383 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is ${R}_{3}:=(-1){R}_{3}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=(-1){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is ${R}_{2}↔{R}_{3}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478453 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186478336 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478453 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75110" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478453 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478453 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that the elementary row operation \n${R}_{1}:=\\frac{5}{2}{R}_{1}$ is applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478453 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e13146e0-974e-5b74-8d7d-df8fb20c3089" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478453 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to find a matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:=\\frac{5}{2}{R}_{1}$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{5}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478461 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186478259 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478461 #edb/ref 1069 "q-110459" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478461 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478461 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider $E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ and a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ Find the row operation that, when applied to $A,$ is equivalent to multiplying $A$ by the given elementary matrix $E$ from the left." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478461 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f636a770-dab5-5ae4-9692-f47eb622812f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186478461 #edb/ref 1074 "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the first row of ${I}_{3}$ and adding $4$ times the third row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+4{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+4{R}_{3}$ to $A.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
